<!--
  CLI Documentation — CompileCommand
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.cli.documentation.CompileCommand
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:blockml="org.blockml.bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:def="org.blockml.bml.definition"
  xmlns:cli="org.blockml.bml.cli"
  xmlns:cliapi="org.blockml.bml.cli.api"
  xmlns:clicap="org.blockml.bml.cli.capability"
  xmlns:clicommand="org.blockml.bml.cli.command"
  xmlns:cliconfig="org.blockml.bml.cli.config"
  xmlns:clidocumentation="org.blockml.bml.cli.documentation"
  xmlns:runtime="org.blockml.bml.compiler.runtime"
  xmlns:framework="org.blockml.bml.framework"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.documentation">

  <name>CompileCommand</name>
  <type>clidocumentation:CompileCommand</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>blockml compile specification</is>

  <documentation><![CDATA[Syntax (V1 minimal CLI):
    blockml compile blockdoc|xsd [--out dir] [--src dir] [--libraries a,b]
    blockml compile fatblock [--include a,b] [--out dir] [--per-package]
    blockml compile file.bml fatblock [--src dir] [--include a,b] [--out dir]

    Default target: blockdoc (CLI12).
    Default outDir: blockdoc (blockdoc), schemas (xsd), invocation directory (fatblock) (CLI13).

    Unsupported target in V1 CLI → exit 2.
    fatblock without file uses package.json blockml.library as host and that
    library directory as --src (CLI14). Missing both file and library → exit 2.
    fatblock --per-package: one {hostFqn}.fat.bml per local package with
    blockml.library (this package and packages/*), all written to the invocation
    directory; not with host file or --src (CLI23).

    Library/corpus targets: one compileToOutput per invocation; --all ignored (CLI19).
    Document target fatblock: writes {hostFqn}.fat.bml with embeddedBlocks at the
    invocation directory.

    After diagnostics, always a status line: Compilation succeeded. Wrote … or
    Compilation failed with K error(s). Empty output without errors:
    Compilation failed: no output files produced.

Printed help:
Usage: blockml compile <target> [--out dir] [--src dir] [--libraries a,b]
       blockml compile fatblock [--include a,b] [--out dir] [--per-package]
       blockml compile <file> <document-target> [--src dir] [--include a,b] [--out dir]
       blockml compile --help

When: a companion is a compile target. Change BML first, then recompile. Do not patch compile output to fix the model. Companions with no target are updated by direct edit after the BML change.

Targets: blockdoc (default), xsd, fatblock. Custom targets via targetPackages.

Flags:
  --out dir         output directory (defaults: blockdoc, schemas, invocation directory)
  --src / --libraries   corpus overrides
  --include a,b     fatblock embed include patterns
  --per-package     one {hostFqn}.fat.bml per local package with blockml.library (fatblock only; not with host file or --src)

fatblock without a host file uses package.json blockml.library as host.

Related: validate.]]></documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="clidocumentation:ValidateCommand" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>

</block>
